Day14
Problem statement: Setup SSL for Nginx (Install, configure and verify)

1. Login into server where we need to install Nginx using ssh, provide password once prompted
        ssh username@hostname
2. Install nginx (Assumed it is CentOS) using below command
        sudo yum install nginx -y
3. It is assumed that we have .crt and .key file required for SSL.
4. Move these files to /etc/nginx/ssl (create if directory not available) using below command
        mv name_of_crt_file /etc/nginx/ssl
        mv name_of_key_file /etc/nginx/ssl
5. Create or overwrite the index.html file in the default Nginx document root
        echo "Welcome!" > /usr/share/nginx/html/index.html
6. Edit the Nginx configuration file (often located at /etc/nginx/nginx.conf or in /etc/nginx/conf.d/). You need to configure a server block to listen on port 443 with SSL enabled. (Note: If there is an existing server block for port 80, you may need to comment it out or adapt the configuration.)
        server {
                listen 443 ssl;
                server_name server_name; # Or the appropriate hostname/IP

                ssl_certificate /etc/nginx/ssl/name_of_crt_file.crt;
                ssl_certificate_key /etc/nginx/ssl/name_of_key_file.key;

        location / {
        root /usr/share/nginx/html;
        index index.html;
        }
    }
7. Restart and enable nginx using below commands
        systemctl restart nginx
        systemctl enable nginx
8. Verify using below curl command
        curl -Ik https://hostname/        